{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu","id":957036,"title":"Forsaken and the Ainu","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T10:27:35-07:00","id":957036,"title":"Forsaken and the Ainu","content":"Someone reminded me of this today, and I was surprised nobody made a thread about it on launch: how does everyone feel about the Tokyo setting stating that most of Japan's werewolves are of Ainu descent? CofD has been pretty adamant from day one about distancing itself from saying various marginalized ethnicities are magical like WoD was so prone to, and this feels like a step backwards to me (to say nothing of how limiting it is narratively).<br /> <br /> Does this leave a bad taste in anyone else's mouth, or just me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-24-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T10:59:06-07:00","id":957045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu#post957036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone reminded me of this today, and I was surprised nobody made a thread about it on launch: how does everyone feel about the Tokyo setting stating that most of Japan's werewolves are of Ainu descent? CofD has been pretty adamant from day one about distancing itself from saying various marginalized ethnicities are magical like WoD was so prone to, and this feels like a step backwards to me (to say nothing of how limiting it is narratively).<br /> <br /> Does this leave a bad taste in anyone else's mouth, or just me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I viewed it as more of a &quot;This is how things are&quot; rather than &quot;This is how things <i>must</i> be&quot;; in other words &quot;While Werewolves aren't tied to ethnic groups, they're still human and thus prone to their own flavor of tribalism, and the Ainu werewolves are the ones who won out here.&quot; Non-Ainu werewolves can still happen, of course, they're just the minority <i>right now</i>.<br /> <br /> You make a compelling argument though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T10:59:19-07:00","id":957046,"title":"","content":"To be fair, they say most Forsaken are Ainu, not that most Ainu are Forsaken. Also that it was more the case historically than it is now. All the same, I did think it was odd. I'd be interested to hear David talk about that decision and why he wrote that into it before I pass any judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:14:08-07:00","id":957055,"title":"","content":"It's just odd to tie the Forsaken down to one ethnic group when the werewolf condition is explicitly not a genetic one in this game.<br /> <br /> It also makes my idea for Meiji Werewolf much harder to execute, which surely doesn't bias me at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:18:26-07:00","id":957058,"title":"","content":"I didn't like it. It seemed like it would fit Apocalypse more than Forsaken, but I'm sure it could be justified through just having more natural-born wolf-blooded for some reason. <br /> <br /> But I get that the Tokyo examples in the books make attempts to be different from the standard set-up, which is good to have even if I don't like how it turns out. And of course, I and anyone else can just choose not to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:22:04-07:00","id":957062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957055#post957055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just odd to tie the Forsaken down to one ethnic group when the werewolf condition is explicitly not a genetic one in this game.<br /> <br /> It also makes my idea for Meiji Werewolf much harder to execute, which surely doesn't bias me at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you <i>could</i> change it so that the Ainu werewolves are the majority <i>exclusively in the modern day</i>, not the past: At some point, there was a *ahem* &quot;mass exodus&quot; of non-Ainu Japanese werewolves, perhaps after the Meiji Period. I did something similar with my Cascadia setting by involving an <i>idigam</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:23:00-07:00","id":957063,"title":"","content":"I haven't picked up Werewolf 2nd edition yet, but is it the Forsaken are mostly Ainu or werewolves are mostly Ainu? That could make a large difference in how I feel about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:29:01-07:00","id":957069,"title":"","content":"I've actually kinda liked it- Tokyo is already a weird setting in many ways, and tying the Uratha to the Ainu made things even weirder, making you think about how and why does a person becomes a werewolf. Considering that it doesn't say that &quot;all Ainu are wolf blooded or werewolves&quot; but that &quot;if someone is a werewolf, than most chances are that he is an Ainu&quot;, it doesn't really makes me feel uncomfortable- but I must admit that things from that kind usually just fly over my head. I mean, someone once had to sit and explain to me what is the problem at CWoD's Gypsies (I was young, but I still don't think it is an excuse)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:31:30-07:00","id":957071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957062#post957062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you <i>could</i> change it so that the Ainu werewolves are the majority <i>exclusively in the modern day</i>, not the past: At some point, there was a *ahem* &quot;mass exodus&quot; of non-Ainu Japanese werewolves, perhaps after the Meiji Period. I did something similar with my Cascadia setting by involving an <i>idigam</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not mistaken, Fallen Blossoms (the Edo period Dark Era) has already established that even in the past, the werewolf-Ainu connection was a &quot;thing&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:40:38-07:00","id":957077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957071#post957071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not mistaken, Fallen Blossoms (the Edo period Dark Era) has already established that even in the past, the werewolf-Ainu connection was a &quot;thing&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>/me whistles as he checks out the Dark Eras book*<br /> <br /> Yep, that's super weird. Okay. I guess since the core book says that &quot;While the proportion of ethnic Japanese werewolves is now no less than among other ethnicities...&quot; you could argue that by the Meiji Period non-Ainu werewolves were on the rise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:44:38-07:00","id":957078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957077#post957077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, that's super weird. Okay. I guess since the core book says that &quot;While the proportion of ethnic Japanese werewolves is now no less than among other ethnicities...&quot; you could argue that by the Meiji Period non-Ainu werewolves were on the rise?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does say one house fell due to the 'scandal.' I guess the nobles thought that someone must have slept with an Ainu, not realizing that people can be chosen at random, and perhaps it was happening more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:08:25-07:00","id":957093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957063#post957063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't picked up Werewolf 2nd edition yet, but is it the Forsaken are mostly Ainu or werewolves are mostly Ainu? That could make a large difference in how I feel about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves. And as mentioned, they're not really mostly Ainu any more, but that's still the stereotype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:17:59-07:00","id":957100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957093#post957093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves. And as mentioned, they're not really mostly Ainu any more, but that's still the stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, that is the more problematic of the two. But without reading the whole thing its hard to judge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:50:30-07:00","id":957122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu#post957036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone reminded me of this today, and I was surprised nobody made a thread about it on launch: how does everyone feel about the Tokyo setting stating that most of Japan's werewolves are of Ainu descent? CofD has been pretty adamant from day one about distancing itself from saying various marginalized ethnicities are magical like WoD was so prone to, and this feels like a step backwards to me (to say nothing of how limiting it is narratively).<br /> <br /> Does this leave a bad taste in anyone else's mouth, or just me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand how this could offend anyone, and I'm a white male. People slander me with impunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:55:13-07:00","id":957131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957122#post957122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't understand how this could offend anyone, and I'm a white male. People slander me with impunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetishizing a real and marginalized ethnic group as being magical dehumanizes them. WoD's treatment of the Romani people (and some loud members of the community defending that) is a large part of why I avoid so much of those games, and it's sad to see CofD regress on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:10:01-07:00","id":957143,"title":"","content":"Based on my research, the Ainu seemed to have stayed in hunter gatherer mode longer then many other ethnic groups did (including Native Americans, given that they actually had an urban civilization before smallpox and the white man decimated it.), as such, it could just be that the Ainu Uratha/wolf-blooded's natural talent at hunting caused them to survive to reproduce more often then non Uratha/wolf-blooded Ainu. It's simple evolution, really, which any supernatural condition that runs in family lines would be subject to. Nothing to do with the Ainu being inherently magical at all.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is based on my pre-existing head canon of Uratha being more common in hunter-gatherer cultures in general (which also results in ADHD being more common than average in Uratha population due to the hunter-farmer hypothesis of ADHD), so feel free to disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:10:06-07:00","id":957144,"title":"","content":"well, I don't see that the writeup makes them Ainu feel fetishized, because that is a local, no longer modern phenomena. I don't get a &quot;Ainu are magical!&quot; feeling from the text, since being a werewolf and being an Ainu are two separate things. It is not that being an Ainu makes you a werewolf, but that for some reason, whatever makes one into a werewolf were more likely to happen among the Ainu. It is the same way I don't feel offended in any way that the descendants of Loew in P:tC 2E are presented as knowing occult secrets and the ability to banish ghosts, demons and other terrors- because I know that Hunter is a thing, and that their abilities and knowledge don't come from them being Jews, but that the descendants of a Kabbalist rabbi are more likely to have such tools to fight the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not the one to judge whether the portrayal of the Ainu-werewolf connection is offensive or not- the ones to makes such judgement are people from Ainu background, and if, in general, Ainu people feel offended, than it is a problem. If they won't feel offended, or maybe even like it, then it is not offending. This is their right to decide something like that, not mine or anyone else (unless the amount of racial stereotyping is very clear, like giving Gypsies the supernatural ability to steal things)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:10:34-07:00","id":957145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957131#post957131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fetishizing a real and marginalized ethnic group as being magical dehumanizes them. WoD's treatment of the Romani people (and some loud members of the community defending that) is a large part of why I avoid so much of those games, and it's sad to see CofD regress on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering populations of Uratha across the globe aren't picky, it would seem that it's the 'ethnic Japanese' that are getting the attention. Less of them are becoming werewolves than everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:15:35-07:00","id":957149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957131#post957131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fetishizing a real and marginalized ethnic group as being magical dehumanizes them. WoD's treatment of the Romani people (and some loud members of the community defending that) is a large part of why I avoid so much of those games, and it's sad to see CofD regress on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest problem with WoD was that it took the most negative stereotypes of groups and applied them to the whole group. The Assamites, who are predominantly Middle-Eastern, are all a bunch of pious assassins and terrorists. The Fianna, who are predominantly Irish, are hyperemotional brawl-happy alcoholics. The Dreamspeakers took every indigenous group in the world and threw them into a Mage Tradition. <br /> <br /> Unless you're something of a Japanophile or watch a decent amount of anime, a lot of people don't even know that the Ainu even exist. And there's also the fact that &quot;all werewolves in Tokyo are Ainu&quot; is acknowledged as an in-universe stereotype. Acknowledging that something is a stereotype is better than perpetuating a stereotype out of malice, or making an ill-conceived attempt at diversity and inclusivity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:29:44-07:00","id":957155,"title":"","content":"I think there's a few factors at play here.<br /> <br /> From a genetic perspective, you can make a solid claim that most people in Japan are of aboriginal ancestry, with central Japan having the least diversity/highest proportion of mainland genes, and the north and south of Japan having the highest levels of genetically observable mixed ancestry. The number of people that actively identify as Ainu is incredibly small, but the number of people in Japan that have Ainu (or at least Jomon) ancestry is very large. To give a comparison to a country that has a bit less cultural baggage on being identified as being of mixed heritage (and thus has much better demographic data) in Mexico, only 7% of the population actively identify as members of one of the indigenous peoples, but 83% of the population are mixed Spanish/indigenous ethnic combinations. Saying that the majority of Mexican werewolves have indigenous ancestry is practically redundant.<br /> <br /> Much like Mexicans are a unique people born of the interbreeding and cultural sharing of indigenous populations with European colonists, the Japanese people (genetically, I'm aware that culturally this is a position many Japanese people reject) are a unique people born of the interbreeding of indigenous populations with colonists from the Korean peninsula. Japan has had a long history of aboriginal erasure, and taboo against mixed ancestry individuals, making it extremely hard to tell exactly how genetically mixed the population really is. It could very well be that the explanation is as simple as most werewolves in Japan of are Ainu descent because most people in the islands share that ancestry on some level.<br /> <br /> Tokyo is also one of the places with the largest Ainu revival communities outside of Hokkaido (which the text highlights). Besides all of the cultural issues they have to overcome in trying to reclaim their cultural identity, they also have to content with a completely unknown factor that most potential members were raised as purely Japanese with zero idea that they have relatively recent Ainu ancestors.<br /> <br /> To me, while my knowledge of all this is extremely academic, the idea mostly comes off as playing with Japanese cultural taboos. The Ainu being associated with werewolves (with people that seem to be completely ethnically Japanese being werewolves and getting dubbed Ainu for it being a thing) makes sense when you consider that the stereotypes of the Ainu by mainstream Japanese culture has a lot of overlap with how Uratha end up operating (the Ainu are stereotyped as being more &quot;wild&quot; and physical, as backwards hunters, and the whole &quot;hairy Ainu&quot; thing combined with the Dalu form).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 08-24-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:43:29-07:00","id":957167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957131#post957131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fetishizing a real and marginalized ethnic group as being magical dehumanizes them. WoD's treatment of the Romani people (and some loud members of the community defending that) is a large part of why I avoid so much of those games, and it's sad to see CofD regress on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain how? The Ainu are a very small ethnic group that most people probably haven't heard of, why wouldn't they want to see themselves in fiction, especially as magical? As stereotypes go that sounds really cool to me.<br /> <br /> PS, Ainu are the only people in the world to be able to be born with golden eyes, if that isn't beautiful and magical I don't know what is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:38:19-07:00","id":957190,"title":"","content":"Reading the section, I tend to get the impression that it's meant to be something untrue that the Uratha of Tokyo believe none the less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957167#post957167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain how? The Ainu are a very small ethnic group that most people probably haven't heard of, why wouldn't they want to see themselves in fiction, especially as magical? As stereotypes go that sounds really cool to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as you yourself are a white male, it's not really your call to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PS, Ainu are the only people in the world to be able to be born with golden eyes, if that isn't beautiful and magical I don't know what is. </div> </div> </div>That's quite creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:51:29-07:00","id":957197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957190#post957190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the section, I tend to get the impression that it's meant to be something untrue that the Uratha of Tokyo believe none the less.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Seeing as you yourself are a white male, it's not really your call to make.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's quite creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my call if I have looked into their culture. An informed outside opionion is as valid as an inside one. Sounds to me like you want to put me in my place. <br /> <br /> My &quot;creepy&quot; comment was a complement calling attention to something unique and cool about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-24-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:54:23-07:00","id":957202,"title":"","content":"Gee, whoever could have foreseen this thread going this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:08:46-07:00","id":957215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957197#post957197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My &quot;creepy&quot; comment was a complement calling attention to something unique and cool about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. That doesn't make it any less creepy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An informed outside opionion is as valid as an inside one. </div> </div> </div>Do you know any Ainu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:24:21-07:00","id":957226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957215#post957215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know. That doesn't make it any less creepy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do you know any Ainu?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's this thing called the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:36:46-07:00","id":957234,"title":"","content":"Well, based on the internet, I can definitely tell you that white males are magical and creepy.<br /> <br /> I'm not a white male, but I've looked into your culture, so I know what I'm talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:42:02-07:00","id":957237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957234#post957234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, based on the internet, I can definitely tell you that white males are magical and creepy.<br /> <br /> I'm not a white male, but I've looked into your culture, so I know what I'm talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you are entitled to your opinion. And white males get one too. See how fair that is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:06:38-07:00","id":957272,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">There is no way this line of discussion is going anywhere good. Drop it, or I will lock the thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T18:40:24-07:00","id":957317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957144#post957144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, I don't see that the writeup makes them Ainu feel fetishized, because that is a local, no longer modern phenomena. I don't get a &quot;Ainu are magical!&quot; feeling from the text, since being a werewolf and being an Ainu are two separate things. It is not that being an Ainu makes you a werewolf, but that for some reason, whatever makes one into a werewolf were more likely to happen among the Ainu. It is the same way I don't feel offended in any way that the descendants of Loew in P:tC 2E are presented as knowing occult secrets and the ability to banish ghosts, demons and other terrors- because I know that Hunter is a thing, and that their abilities and knowledge don't come from them being Jews, but that the descendants of a Kabbalist rabbi are more likely to have such tools to fight the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not the one to judge whether the portrayal of the Ainu-werewolf connection is offensive or not- the ones to makes such judgement are people from Ainu background, and if, in general, Ainu people feel offended, than it is a problem. If they won't feel offended, or maybe even like it, then it is not offending. This is their right to decide something like that, not mine or anyone else (unless the amount of racial stereotyping is very clear, like giving Gypsies the supernatural ability to steal things)</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, there aren't that many Ainu people around compared to the numbers of Wajin, so having substantial numbers of Uratha be descended from Ainu would tend to make said werewolves much more noticeable. If you're holding to one werewolf per 200k humans, and just take the entirety of Japan's population but make it so that they all fall into descent alongside a much smaller pool of likely at most 200K, things are going to get very crowded in one ethnic group, at about 650 times the expected frequency of werewolves (expected # of Uratha given the entire Japanese population is 650; expected # of Uratha given the Ainu population, with no Wajin counted, is 1 at the most).<br /> <br /> Also, does the preference for Ainu hold with the Kuriles, Sakhalins, and Kamchatka as well? That;'d get even more crowded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:06:16-07:00","id":957356,"title":"","content":"I don't really get the argument- why would the amount of Ainu people would influence whether it dehumanize the Ainu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:23:01-07:00","id":957367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957317#post957317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, there aren't that many Ainu people around compared to the numbers of Wajin, so having substantial numbers of Uratha be descended from Ainu would tend to make said werewolves much more noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd point back to my last post though. There aren't that man recognized Ainu people, because there's been centuries of erasure of the idea of mixed Ainu-Wajin people existing (even if there's evidence that a huge portion of the population is likely mixed). And there's no social pressure in Japan to take genetic tests and find out you're not purely Wajin like there is in the US right now to use a genetic check to explore your ancestral diversity. <br /> <br /> It's a key phrasing in the text that it says, &quot;Ainu descent,&quot; which is a very large if unrecognized group, not just being a recognized Ainu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:26:43-07:00","id":957370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957367#post957367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's no social pressure in Japan to take genetic tests and find out you're not purely Wajin like there is in the US right now to use a genetic check to explore your ancestral diversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a thing here? I'm not doubting, just curious. The only incident I heard about it was some white supremacist on a talk show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:26:28-07:00","id":957394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957370#post957370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a thing here? I'm not doubting, just curious. The only incident I heard about it was some white supremacist on a talk show.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much a social pressure so much that America is currently in the middle of a long running fascination with genealogy and finding your roots that originally began in the African American and Mormon communities and has since gone mainstream. I have an ancestry account but haven't gotten the DNA test yet, maybe I will someday, if only to see if that old family claim to be part Cherokee is real or not (I located the records of the many greats grand mother who was supposedly half Cherokee, but her parents don't seem to have any records that the ancestry people can find).<br /> <br /> I want to believe it's real, but here in the south there was a period where confederacy supporters claimed the Cherokee as ancestors due to a romanticized view of the Cherokee as the first people of the south to be &quot;oppressed by the tyrannical federal government&quot; and the fact that ancestry has shown that I have slave owners in my family tree means they may hav been making that claim those same reasons. Ancestry also told me that my 5th great-grandparents on my maternal grandfather's side were cousins.<br /> <br /> So yeah, not everyone who gets into genealogy here in the US finds good stuff about their family, sometimes you get guys like me who open a door to the family skeleton closet and can't shut it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T22:13:57-07:00","id":957413,"title":"","content":"It might not be super wide spread, but there's national commercial campaigns in the US to get your DNA tested to find out your ethnic background. That counts as social pressure in my book, even if it's a specific form of it. <br /> <br /> I've never bothered with it because I did the tests on myself in genetics class and found out... absolutely nothing I didn't know, and all of my direct ancestors came to the US in the 30s from countries that didn't exactly have maintaining our genealogy paperwork as a high priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T22:21:06-07:00","id":957415,"title":"","content":"Huh, interesting. I was adopted, and while we've found out about my mother she died a few years after I was born and no one alive knows anything worthwhile about my father.<br /> <br /> Anyways, sorry for the derail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T22:32:47-07:00","id":957419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957367#post957367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd point back to my last post though. There aren't that man recognized Ainu people, because there's been centuries of erasure of the idea of mixed Ainu-Wajin people existing (even if there's evidence that a huge portion of the population is likely mixed). And there's no social pressure in Japan to take genetic tests and find out you're not purely Wajin like there is in the US right now to use a genetic check to explore your ancestral diversity.<br /> <br /> It's a key phrasing in the text that it says, &quot;Ainu descent,&quot; which is a very large if unrecognized group, not just being a recognized Ainu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did use the high estimate; the low one sits at only 25K, which we probably both agree is far too low. On the other hand, is there data showing widespread intermarriage like in Mexico? I haven't managed to find anything that significant. I'm getting the feeling that we're also bumping into territory that experts are still arguing over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:03:23-07:00","id":957456,"title":"","content":"From everything I've read, it's a lot less, &quot;experts are still arguing over,&quot; and a lot more, &quot;experts are frustrated because social taboos are blocking research.&quot; What little evidence there is points to large scale interbreeding (not intermarriage, which implies both partners maintained their ethnic identify, as many Ainu were historically forced/coerced into giving up their culture so their children could be raised Wajin and persecution free) due to unique genotypes only found in the Ainu people showing up in people that identify as purely Wajin, but there's not enough sample size to push it forward; and it's hard to get a sample size when it amounts to, &quot;take a test to prove you're a member of a persecuted minority.&quot; The experts all want to prove their various positions, but the mainstream society is very clearly much happier not knowing.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind we're talking about ethnic groups that coexisted in the Japanese islands for thousands of years before concepts of racial purity among the Wajin took root and large scale ethnic and cultural erasure took place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:19:41-07:00","id":957460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957122#post957122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand how this could offend anyone, and I'm a white male. People slander me with impunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind...blown...for many reasons - some bad but also good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I guess I never made the connection between WoD's Romani and CofD's Ainu. I think it handled far more tactfully than the former, whatever peoples' disagreements are","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T21:58:25-07:00","id":958058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957155#post957155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a few factors at play here.<br /> <br /> From a genetic perspective, you can make a solid claim that most people in Japan are of aboriginal ancestry, with central Japan having the least diversity/highest proportion of mainland genes, and the north and south of Japan having the highest levels of genetically observable mixed ancestry. The number of people that actively identify as Ainu is incredibly small, but the number of people in Japan that have Ainu (or at least Jomon) ancestry is very large. To give a comparison to a country that has a bit less cultural baggage on being identified as being of mixed heritage (and thus has much better demographic data) in Mexico, only 7% of the population actively identify as members of one of the indigenous peoples, but 83% of the population are mixed Spanish/indigenous ethnic combinations. Saying that the majority of Mexican werewolves have indigenous ancestry is practically redundant.<br /> <br /> Much like Mexicans are a unique people born of the interbreeding and cultural sharing of indigenous populations with European colonists, the Japanese people (genetically, I'm aware that culturally this is a position many Japanese people reject) are a unique people born of the interbreeding of indigenous populations with colonists from the Korean peninsula. Japan has had a long history of aboriginal erasure, and taboo against mixed ancestry individuals, making it extremely hard to tell exactly how genetically mixed the population really is. It could very well be that the explanation is as simple as most werewolves in Japan of are Ainu descent because most people in the islands share that ancestry on some level.<br /> <br /> Tokyo is also one of the places with the largest Ainu revival communities outside of Hokkaido (which the text highlights). Besides all of the cultural issues they have to overcome in trying to reclaim their cultural identity, they also have to content with a completely unknown factor that most potential members were raised as purely Japanese with zero idea that they have relatively recent Ainu ancestors.<br /> <br /> To me, while my knowledge of all this is extremely academic, the idea mostly comes off as playing with Japanese cultural taboos. The Ainu being associated with werewolves (with people that seem to be completely ethnically Japanese being werewolves and getting dubbed Ainu for it being a thing) makes sense when you consider that the stereotypes of the Ainu by mainstream Japanese culture has a lot of overlap with how Uratha end up operating (the Ainu are stereotyped as being more &quot;wild&quot; and physical, as backwards hunters, and the whole &quot;hairy Ainu&quot; thing combined with the Dalu form).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all pretty well-said. And closely lined up with my thinking on the matter.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know how explicit I made it, but my thought was that there WERE other Japanese werewolves (I think I mention that in Dark Eras, in fact). But for some reason, they just... stopped happening. Like with literal Japanese Wolves, they stopped being a thing. <br /> <br /> I don't look at it as if the Ainu are &quot;magical&quot;. Quite the opposite. People all over the world become Uratha. Japanese people not of Ainu heritage tend to not become Uratha. Ainu aren't significantly more likely to become Uratha - but when they're the only ones in the area that consistently do, it perhaps looks like it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T02:31:19-07:00","id":958119,"title":"","content":"I don't see it as any different to any other thing involving cultures in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> As long as it doesn't make statements about the Ainu people as a whole or get into any genuinely racist territory, it remains just a little tidbit of information. While I can see how it could be problematic, I wouldn't really compare it to the Gypsies book, or even the Tribes of Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Note that I'm probably not the best person to judge if there are any problems, considering I wasn't even familiar with what 'Ainu' meant until I read it in Werewolf and subsequently researched the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 08-26-2016, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T04:28:04-07:00","id":958137,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's not a good analogy, but couldn't this topic's claim be applied to the entirety of <b>Mummy: the Curse</b>?<br /> <br /> Even if it's a fictional empire at the dawn of history, clearly Irem and its mythology draws heavily on later Egyptian beliefs, and <i>depends</i> on superstition created by Hollywood of all things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:28:06-07:00","id":958162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu#post957036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone reminded me of this today, and I was surprised nobody made a thread about it on launch: how does everyone feel about the Tokyo setting stating that most of Japan's werewolves are of Ainu descent? CofD has been pretty adamant from day one about distancing itself from saying various marginalized ethnicities are magical like WoD was so prone to, and this feels like a step backwards to me (to say nothing of how limiting it is narratively).<br /> <br /> Does this leave a bad taste in anyone else's mouth, or just me?</div> </div> </div> </div>It bothers me. Mostly because it limits the stories you can tell about ethnic Japanese people.<br /> It is the story option limits that really annoy me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:34:41-07:00","id":958192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=958162#post958162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It bothers me. Mostly because it limits the stories you can tell about ethnic Japanese people.<br /> It is the story option limits that really annoy me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It provides a framework for you to pick and choose setting elements you like or don't. If CofD is a toolbox nothing is really cannon. I never would have thought of using the Ainu in a Tokyo game if it weren't for the idea they gave. I might be using them in a different way, but I won't complain for them giving me ideas. Your supposed to change the setting for your game. This isn't old world of darkness where the meta plot hedges you in. <br /> <br /> In a nut shell. How can being given ideas you could use LIMIT you? I really don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-26-2016, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:55:28-07:00","id":958202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957063#post957063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't picked up Werewolf 2nd edition yet, but is it the Forsaken are mostly Ainu or werewolves are mostly Ainu? That could make a large difference in how I feel about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Forsaken were Ainu in past times, and are still thought to be by the Japanese in the optional Tokyo setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:03:17-07:00","id":958205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957413#post957413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might not be super wide spread, but there's national commercial campaigns in the US to get your DNA tested to find out your ethnic background. That counts as social pressure in my book, even if it's a specific form of it. <br /> <br /> I've never bothered with it because I did the tests on myself in genetics class and found out... absolutely nothing I didn't know, and all of my direct ancestors came to the US in the 30s from countries that didn't exactly have maintaining our genealogy paperwork as a high priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was just ancestory.com commercials to advertise their web site. Some old people are interested in it, seemed pretty interesting to my dad, and sort of pointless to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:06:50-07:00","id":958210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=958162#post958162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It bothers me. Mostly because it limits the stories you can tell about ethnic Japanese people.<br /> It is the story option limits that really annoy me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to just sing the 'optional tookbox games' song, but I will say that it's not like the <b>Werewolf</b> setting for Tokyo hinges on it if you want to change or remove this idea. It's not like Tokyo's Werewolf society comes undone and you the GM have to rebuild it.<br /> <br /> The Tokyo setting is built around Japanese culture. &quot;Hey, let's be inclusive and mention the Ainu because we're inclusive! Okay, well we can't make them have tendencies towards a given splat because people will be upset, so we'll just say that the Ainu exist and they are equally every splat&quot; really doesn't make the word-count worthwhile","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:11:39-07:00","id":958212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=958210#post958210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to just sing the 'optional tookbox games' song, but I will say that it's not like the <b>Werewolf</b> setting for Tokyo hinges on it if you want to change or remove this idea. It's not like Tokyo's Werewolf society comes undone and you the GM have to rebuild it.<br /> <br /> The Tokyo setting is built around Japanese culture. &quot;Hey, let's be inclusive and mention the Ainu because we're inclusive! Okay, well we can't make them have tendencies towards a given splat because people will be upset, so we'll just say that the Ainu exist and they are equally every splat&quot; really doesn't make the word-count worthwhile</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean if you want to include them then you need some context to do so. I'm trying to think of any way they could be named dropped without saying something in general about them. If you can't do that, there really isn't a way you could include them at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:26:19-07:00","id":958220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=958202#post958202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of the Forsaken were Ainu in past times, and are still thought to be by the Japanese in the optional Tokyo setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is important. It's not an enforced limitation - it's mostly a trend and perceived limitation in-setting. And it's not even a remarkably important one. It's mostly there to shake up the way they organize in that particular setting. <br /> <br /> Most of the Tokyo chapters I've written are sort of, &quot;what if this weird thing were true?&quot; Then I sort of explore that and play with it. It's no more limiting than, say, the Vampire chapter if you believe in your heart of hearts that the Masquerade is an absolute law that, if broken, means the end of vampires. It's speculative fiction within speculative fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:53:57-07:00","id":958364,"title":"","content":"It's also... kind of impossible to write up a sample setting and not, &quot;limit story options,&quot; in some fashion. The second an author for one of the sample settings decides that Anchorage has a relatively stable Protectorate built on a core group of Packs that share common indigenous ancestry that's unified them since European settlement, a whole set of story possibilities is out the window. But if you don't do this... what value do these samples have? They'd just become vague descriptions of a place with a bunch of possible story hooks that don't illustrate different ways Uratha live and interact with their world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:34:21-07:00","id":958891,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Oop.s this conversations was supposed to be dropped. Did not know at time of posting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-27-2016, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T18:10:38-07:00","id":958992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=958364#post958364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also... kind of impossible to write up a sample setting and not, &quot;limit story options,&quot; in some fashion. The second an author for one of the sample settings decides that Anchorage has a relatively stable Protectorate built on a core group of Packs that share common indigenous ancestry that's unified them since European settlement, a whole set of story possibilities is out the window. But if you don't do this... what value do these samples have? They'd just become vague descriptions of a place with a bunch of possible story hooks that don't illustrate different ways Uratha live and interact with their world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, my hunter write up for the city of Savannah is based on the idea that because Savannah's supernatural reputation is such a tourist draw that bring a bunch of money to the city, the local hunter compacts and the local agents of the conspiracies only kill the worst offenders among the monsters, everything else is about pushing the limits of the masquerade to drive up tourism. Obviously, having a city where the hunters have decided that having at least a few monsters around is needed for the setting's economic health rules out stories involving more warlike hunters, but if you don't like that, then don't play in my Savannah setting and go for a setting that does support that.<br /> <br /> The setting of a story always rules out certain possibilities, that's part of having a setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:54:16-07:00","id":959246,"title":"","content":"That sounds quite interesting, care to share? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> EDIT: I suppose the trick is being one of the attractions and so be considered useful to have a nice life as a supernatural in Savannah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:30:36-07:00","id":959263,"title":"","content":"I'd also love to see what you have for Savannah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:44:37-07:00","id":959355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=959246#post959246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds quite interesting, care to share? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> EDIT: I suppose the trick is being one of the attractions and so be considered useful to have a nice life as a supernatural in Savannah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my full write up is trapped on my old craptop (crappy laptop) with the busted battery, but since you asked, here is a brief bullet points summary to hold you guys over until I can rewrite it.<ul><li>TFV and VASCU agree that the supernatural is needed for Savannah to thrive, what they know that the other hunter groups don't is that real reason Sherman didn't burn Savannah is that the city is a major junction point for the flow of occult energies across America and burning it would have had nasty effects across the country, thus why TFV paid the local magi to magically fireproof the historic districts where most the energy flows through. For some reason, supernatural abilities in Savannah often manifest younger than usual, perhaps due to the excess of occult energies in the city, so the government compacts include an education department group that manages Georgia's most unique charter schools through a front company funded by local monsters. One of the rules that TFV has that the local monsters must follow is that Pinke Masters' Bar (a frequent stip for presidential campaigns in Georgia is off limits during election years.</li> <li>The Georgia Historic Society has a secret division dedicated to learning the real occult history of Georgia, this compact is one of the major forces in the &quot;push the limits of the masquerade to drive up tourism&quot; plan, along with the 6th Sense Savannah ghost tour company, which researches local ghost stories to add to their tours, and sometimes works with the local sin eaters make sure the ghosts will not be a threat to their customers. The Historic society also interviews older supernaturals that witnessed important events in Georgia's history and really only kills monsters if they become a threat to the city at large.</li> <li>The fallout from the downfall of former police chief Willie Lovett has ended the Carthian regime in Savannah, since it had strong ties to the local African American political machine that had many of it's members thrown out of office due to public fury over Lovett's blatant corruption. The deposed Carthains that were most connected to Lovett are being swamped in the legal system by the famous local lawyer/ hunter Jamie Casino. Casino is a lay member of the Malleus Maleficarum who fights with a literal hammer when his lawyer skills don't work, but is really only a hunter so he can avenge his brother's death, which Lovett attempted to sweep under the rug at the request the Carthain prefect who had him killed. He is not sure if he wants to keep up the vigil after he gets that revenge. Many other supernatural and hunter groups have interests in the Lovett scandal one way or another.</li> <li>The old yellow fever tunnels beneath the city have become something of a supernatural neutral zone/market/hangout. The Nosferatu Lance archbishop who took over after the Carthians fell makes his home here. One of his rules for the local kindred is that the girl scouts are absolutely off limits, which the local werewolves also enforce.</li> <li>The Lady Chablis and her friends at club one come down hard on anyone in Savannah's supernaturally aware community that abuses the local LGBT community. Those in Savannah who know of the astral realm suspect she may have truly merged with (as opposed to being possessed by) her astral symbol of herself, which would help explain why she manages to look so young at her age. Some of the drag queens she employees at club one are themselves supernatural, so it isn't impossible that she has some way of keeping herself young without being a ghoul.</li> <li>The Les <i>Myst\u00e8res</i> used to meet in colonial park cemetery for their rites, but the media freakout resulting from the discovery of the remains of sacrificed animals by a local jogger prompted the historic society and TFV to lock up the cemetery at night.</li> <li>The jagged crescent is the main ascending ones presence in Savannah, selling drugs to the SCAD students makes a good deal of money for them. But they and the night watch took a beating when the ties of their gangs to Lovett (they were amoung the gangs that helped the corrupt anti-drug taskforce deal drugs out of the evidence lockers and several of their leaders were jailed as a result of the officers cutting peal deals).</li> <li>The Loyalists of Thule and the Aegis Kun Doru were kicked out of Savannah on their sliced up asses after they attempted to steal various documents and historic relics from the Historic society.</li> <li>The younger Ashwood Abbey and Network zero members in Savannah are surprising cozy with each other, which probably has to do with most of them being SCAD students, with the zeroes being mostly film students.</li> <li>The fact that Savannah's economy is mostly based on, tourism, manufacturing, the military and shipping means the Union, TFV and the local compacts mentioned above are over represented among the local hunter, with Null Mysteriis and the Cheiron group underrepresented. The Long night and MM are also over represented, but the long night in the town is divided along racial lines (and this has only gotten worse since the Lovett scandal) and the MM was forced to go along with the historic society's plans in the aftermath of the local catholic sex abuse scandal following the Boston scandal.</li> </ul><br /> That's it for now. The werewolves, changelings, beasts and magi will come later. as will the Lucifuge:.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-28-2016, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T12:22:20-07:00","id":959367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=959246#post959246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I suppose the trick is being one of the attractions and so be considered useful to have a nice life as a supernatural in Savannah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the sin eaters in particular live a very comfortable live, compared to their usual low class origins.One sin eater working in the local tourist sector, who officially works as the janitor at the famous 17Hundred90 inn, earned quite a fat pay raise when he got the inns resident ghost Anna, who is well known for harassing female guests, to mess with Miley Cryus's boots and clothing while she was staying there. When Miley tweeted about her ghost story, it brought even more guests to the haunted inn.<br /> <br /> Of course, the werewolves make decent money too, since most mortals wouldn't be able to tell the works of a spirit apart from those of a ghost. But they make their real money off their control of the moon river brewing company, held in common by the protectorate, The building the brewery is housed in is a locus home to many spirits of violence due to the building's past as a seedy bar/hotel in the 1800s. The historic society and TFV pay them to keep the spirits in the building and away from the streets where they might inflame the crime caused by Lovett's corruption.<br /> <br /> The changelings, for their part, hold their freehold meetings at the pirate house (which used to be the site of many kidnappings by both the British navy and the True Fae in the early days of the city) and even have a court system where each court, (called a crew in tow) is themed after a famous pirate from history or fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-28-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:30:19-07:00","id":959482,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Hey folks, I expect a certain amount of topic drift, but this tangent is getting to the point where it should probably move to its own thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:37:23-07:00","id":959523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=959482#post959482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Hey folks, I expect a certain amount of topic drift, but this tangent is getting to the point where it should probably move to its own thread.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I already set up a new thread for my write up <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T20:16:24-07:00","id":963069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=957394#post957394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Ancestry also told me that my 5th great-grandparents on my maternal grandfather's side were cousins.<br /> <br /> So yeah, not everyone who gets into genealogy here in the US finds good stuff about their family, sometimes you get guys like me who open a door to the family skeleton closet and can't shut it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you are referring to the slave ownership when you say &quot;skeletons in the closet&quot;. Cousin marriage is hardly offensive and actually prevalent in many parts of the world.<br /> <br /> I'm married to my first-cousin (paternal side). We have two kids. And yes they have ordinary health.<br /> <br /> My great grandparents on my maternal side were first cousins. They had fourteen (yes 14) kids. All of them ordinary.<br /> <br /> The risk increase for genetic setbacks is little to non appreciable compared to non related pairing.<br /> <br /> It is just a stupid social taboo. I shouldn't get frustrated by this, as it is such a common viewpoint, but hey, I'm human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 09-03-2016, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T20:51:39-07:00","id":963078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=963069#post963069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope you are referring to the slave ownership when you say &quot;skeletons in the closet&quot;. Cousin marriage is hardly offensive and actually prevalent in many parts of the world.<br /> <br /> I'm married to my first-cousin (paternal side). We have two kids. And yes they have ordinary health.<br /> <br /> My great grandparents on my maternal side were first cousins. They had fourteen (yes 14) kids. All of them ordinary.<br /> <br /> The risk increase for genetic setbacks is little to non appreciable compared to non related pairing.<br /> <br /> It is just a stupid social taboo. I shouldn't get frustrated by this, as it is such a common viewpoint, but hey, I'm human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was technically referring to both, along with the other many greats grandfather that came some time after the slave owners who killed a guy and ran away to Kansas to avoid the law, and then started a new family under a fake name. My grandma met our Kansas half cousins and she found out about that. My family closet has many, many skeletons of various degrees of severity and all the stuff I mentioned was just my mother's side, don't even ask about my father's side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T21:11:17-07:00","id":963083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m